  "instructions": [
    "Heat a heavy-bottomed pot over medium heat and add olive oil.",
    "Add sliced onion and cook until translucent, about 5 minutes.",
    "Stir in minced garlic, grated ginger, cumin, coriander, paprika, cinnamon, turmeric, and oregano, and sauté for 2 minutes until fragrant.",
    "Add the tomatoes, wine, and a pinch of salt, then cover and simmer for 15 minutes to allow the flavors to meld.",
    "Break up the tomatoes with a spoon and stir in the chickpeas, reducing the heat to low.",
    "Cover and cook the tagine for an additional 20 minutes, letting the sauce thicken and the tomatoes soften.",
    "Remove the pot from heat and stir in chopped parsley and cilantro for brightness.",
    "Serve the tagine hot over a bed of couscous or plain rice, and garnish with extra herbs if desired."
